      "id": "536k7t5",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Background of Indian National Movement"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The Indian National Movement progressed through distinct phases: Moderate Phase (1885–1905), Extremist Phase (1905–1919), and Gandhian Phase.",
        "Key anti-colonial mass mobilizations included the Swadeshi Movement, Non-Cooperation Movement (1920–1922), Civil Disobedience Movement (1930–1934), and Quit India Movement (1942).",
        "The Home Rule Movement in 1916 played a crucial role in building momentum for self-rule prior to Gandhian mass movements.",
        "The cumulative impact of these movements ultimately culminated in the Independence of India."
      ],
      "id": "wdx5dfl"
    },
